er length␀A steel E string is about 0.4 g/m.␀␀g/m␀I = P/(4*pi*r^2)␀␀␀␀Intensity␀␀␀At distance r. Sunlight on Earth is 1361 W/m^2.␀Source power␀␀␀␀Radiated evenly every way.␀␀From the source.␀␀␀␀L = 20*log10(p/p0)␀␀1 Pa is 94 dB, which is how mics are calibrated.␀␀␀␀Sound pressure␀␀RMS.␀␀␀␀p0␀␀p_{0}␀␀␀Reference␀␀␀20 uPa in air.␀␀L = 10*log10(I/I0)␀␀Talking 60 dB, a rock band 110 dB.␀␀Sound power per area.␀␀␀I0␀␀I_{0}␀␀␀The threshold of hearing, 1e-12 W/m^2.␀␀fo = fs*(c + vo)/(c - vs)␀␀␀f_{o}␀␀␀Heard frequency␀At the listener.␀␀␀␀fs␀␀f_{s}␀␀␀Source frequency␀␀␀␀As sent.␀␀␀␀vo␀␀v_{o}␀␀␀Listener speed␀␀Positive towards the source.␀␀␀␀vs␀␀v_{s}␀␀␀Source speed␀␀␀␀Positive towards the listener. Below the wave speed.␀␀␀␀Sound in air 343 m/s.␀␀␀Air 20 C=343|Air 0 C=331|Helium=1007|Water=1482|Seawater=1522|Glass=5640|Steel=5960|Aluminium=6420␀␀v = f*lambda␀␀␀␀Sound in air 343 m/s, light 3e8 m/s.␀␀␀␀Cycles per second. Concert A is 440 Hz.␀Crest to crest.␀Electrical␀␀Ohm's law, power, R C L, AC␀Electronics & radio␀Timing, filters, op-amps, dB, antennas␀␀Fields & magnetism␀␀Charge, coils, magnets␀␀Motion␀␀Speed, acceleration, projectiles␀␀␀␀Forces & energy␀Newton, friction, work, springs␀Rotation & machines␀Torque, shafts, gears, levers␀␀␀Materials & structures␀␀Stress, beams, shafts, expansion␀␀␀␀Fluids␀␀Pressure, flow, drag␀␀␀␀Heat & gases␀␀␀␀Gas laws, heat flow, engines␀␀␀␀Waves & sound␀␀␀Frequency, decibels, Doppler␀␀␀␀Light & optics␀␀Lenses, refraction, photons␀Atoms & relativity␀␀E = mc^2, matter waves, levels␀␀Gravity & space␀Orbits, escape, rockets␀Chemistry␀␀␀Moles, pH, rates, decay␀Geometry␀␀␀␀Shapes, solids, triangles␀␀␀atan2␀␀␀log␀sqrt␀␀␀␀(3.141592653589793)␀Âµ␀␀Needs ␀␀ from 0 to 90 deg␀␀␀ above 0␀␀␀␀cbrt␀␀␀␀log10␀␀␀ln␀␀tan␀abs␀exp␀sin␀asin␀␀␀␀cos␀acos␀␀␀␀atan␀␀␀␀sinh␀␀␀␀asinh␀␀␀cosh␀␀␀␀acosh␀␀␀tanh␀␀␀␀atanh␀␀␀No real solution for ␀␀␀These values don't fit together␀Two solutions: showing the positive one␀Two solutions: showing the smaller one␀␀Two solutions: showing